# =============================================================================
# geometry dogbone_2D_L1100um_W150um_wc40um_lens90flat_eps0.86um.opts   (preprocess/build_geometry_dogbone.py)
# Plan type 6 (make_type6_inputs.py, 2026-11-12): dog-bone pore, neck wc = 40 um, lens faces at 90 deg.
#
# Dog-bone pore: wide sections W = 150.0 um, straight neck wc = 40.0 um on
# x = 400.0-700.0 um, C-infinity shoulders 100.0 um long (steepest wall
# slope 1.100); walls flat on x = 0-300.0 and 800.0-1100.0 um.
# The walls are in the mesh (dogbone_wc40um.dat); y0 and y1 are wall faces, x0 and x1 are
# the pore ends.
#
# The -Ly / default flat walls below are ONLY for the initial-condition layout.
# The lens sits where the walls are exactly flat (y = 0 and y = W), so the IC
# is exact there; elsewhere the IC is ice-free. See the builder's docstring.
# Postprocessing must take wall positions from the mesh or from this line:
# DOGBONE: W 1.500000e-04 wc 4.000000e-05 x_n0 4.000000e-04 x_n1 7.000000e-04 shoulder 1.000000e-04
#
# Lens: apexes on the axis x = 875.0-1025.0 um, ice x = 875.0-1025.0 um,
# exactly flat faces (90 deg; -ice_flat_*, ice on x = 875.0-1025.0 um at every y).
# eps 8.5840e-07 m (production value, issue 1), h = eps/sqrt(2): Nx 1813, Ny 248.
# =============================================================================
# DOF_GRID: 1815 250
-geom_file inputs/geometry/meshes/dogbone_wc40um.dat
-p 2
-C 1
-ic_type multi_grains
-dim 2
-Lx 1.100000e-03
-Ly 1.500000e-04
-Lz 0
-ice_flat_x 9.500000e-04
-ice_flat_R 7.500000e-05
-ice_flat_height 3.000000e-04
-delt_t 1.0e-4
-eps 8.5840e-07
-eps_valid_temp -20
-periodic 0
-wall_faces y0,y1
-dtmax 1.3412e+03
